{{!-- A2, "three-column grid", on a tag archive: every post as an equal card.

	{{> "tag/a2"}}

No lead story here, which is the whole of what distinguishes this layout from A1: the design's
card grid gives every post in the subject the same weight, so there is nothing for the first row
to be first at, and nothing that changes on page 2.

The grid's track is 330px rather than the Feed's 320px — the design sets a slightly wider card
on an archive that carries fewer posts. --}}
<section
	id="posts"
	aria-label="{{t "Posts"}}"
	class="container pt-2">
	<div class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(330px,100%),1fr))] gap-x-10 gap-y-13">
		{{#foreach posts}}
			{{> "archive/card"}}
		{{else}}
			<p class="font-body text-muted">{{t "Nothing filed under this tag yet."}}</p>
		{{/foreach}}
	</div>
</section>
